From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:37:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add compatibility mode for plugins not marked as Folia
 supported

Plugins without folia-supported: true were refused, and the
BukkitScheduler threw UnsupportedOperationException for every task.
Plugins listed under compat.plugins in tessera.yml (or "*") are now
loaded with a warning, and their BukkitScheduler tasks are accepted:
sync tasks run on the global region thread, async tasks on the Bukkit
async pool, with task ids, cancelling, isQueued and getPendingTasks
working as on Paper. Their tasks are cancelled when the plugin is
disabled. Plugins marked as Folia supported see no change, and with
nothing listed the scheduler still throws.

Changing blocks or entities from such a task still fails off the
owning region thread; that is handled separately.

